.into(), rhs.into(), RelOp::Le)\n    }\n\n    /// D-LAYOUT1 / D-LAYOUT-GATES1 (GATE 1): `lhs == rhs` between layout values.\n    /// Named `eq_` (not `eq`) to stay clear of `PartialEq::eq`.\n    pub fn eq_(lhs: impl Into<LinExpr>, rhs: impl Into<LinExpr>) -> Constraint {\n        make_constraint(lhs.into(), rhs.into(), RelOp::Eq)\n    }\n}\n// jet:cached-runtime-end\n/* jet-corelib-r10 source=1bbebe2f79742ef90259e2b7ce70dfbf3de7696bf496269c310e73a4c36f6cb1 closure=61219511858af41d69442a5ecb0b1e80fb669bcbd979df4c03588a7bc301570d len=3305313 fp=59c527df75d80735918694f08cb25a3a046ec634b77dc2b88ecec107e527aeae */\n\nmod jet_xml_pull {\n//! Shared std-only encoding engines compiled by generated and comptime tiers.\n//! The primary engine here is the XML 1.0 pull tokenizer.\n\nuse std::collections::{BTreeMap, BTreeSet};\n\n/// D-ENCBASE-STRICT1=A edition-2026 compatibility engine. This module lives in\n/// the existing std-only generated/comptime seam so both tiers compile exactly\n/// one decoder source. Edition 2027 strict defaults remain toolchain-gated.\npub mod base_encoding_2026 {\n    fn base64_digit(byte: u8) -> Option<u8> {\n        match byte {\n            b'A'..=b'Z' => Some(byte - b'A'),\n            b'a'..=b'z' => Some(byte - b'a' + 26),\n            b'0'..=b'9' => Some(byte - b'0' + 52),\n            b'+' => Some(62),\n            b'/' => Some(63),\n            _ => None,\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn historical_aot(text: &str) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {\n        let input: Vec<u8> = text.bytes().filter(|&b| !b.is_ascii_whitespace()).collect();\n        if input.len() % 4 != 0 {\n            return None;\n        }\n        let mut out = Vec::with_capacity(input.len() / 4 * 3);\n        for chunk in input.chunks(4) {\n            let a = base64_digit(chunk[0])?;\n            let b = base64_digit(chunk[1])?;\n            out.push((a << 2) | (b >> 4));\n            if chunk[2] != b'=' {\n                let c = base64_digit(chunk[2])?;\n                out.push((b <<